hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20582","'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Qatadah ibn Milhan al-Qaysi, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to fast the white nights: thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen, and said: They are like fasting the whole year."
"20583","'Arim narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: And my father narrated from al-'Ala' ibn 'Umayr, he said: I was with Qatadah ibn Milhan when he was dying, and a man passed at the far end of the house, and I saw him in Qatadah's face - he said: And whenever I saw him it was as if oil was on his face - he said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had wiped over his face."
"20584","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: Yahya ibn Ma'in and Huraym Abu Hamzah narrated to us, they said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, then he mentioned the like of it."
"20585","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to me, from 'Abd al-Malik, a man from Banu Qays ibn Tha'labah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order them to fast the white days, saying: They are the fast of the month, or he said: The year."
"20586","Rawh narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Qatadah ibn Milhan al-Qaysi, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to fast the white nights: thirteen, fourteen, and fifteen, saying: They are like the whole year."
"20587","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I heard 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Minhal narrating from his father, he said: And he was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to order us to fast the three white days, saying: They are the fast of the whole year."
